    "sections": {
        "description": "<p><strong>This is a lightweight CAPTCHA plugin for WordPress and WooCommerce.</strong><br />\n★★★★★</p>\n<p>The free version supports the &#8220;I\\&#8217;m not a robot&#8221; Checkbox from Google reCAPTCHA.</p>\n<p>The premius version supports:-<br />\n&#8211; Invisible reCAPTCHA V2.<br />\n&#8211; Score based reCAPTCHA V3.<br />\n&#8211; Cloudflare Turnstile.</p>\n<p>Both versions allow you to protect your:-</p>\n<ul>\n<li>WordPress / WooCommerce login forms.</li>\n<li>WordPress / WooCommerce / BuddyPress registration forms.</li>\n<li>WordPress / WooCommerce lost password forms.</li>\n<li>WordPress / WooCommerce reset password forms.</li>\n<li>WordPress comment forms.</li>\n<li>WooCommerce checkout forms.</li>\n<li>Noptin newsletter subscription form.</li>\n<li>BBPress new topic and reply forms.</li>\n<li>BuddyPress new group forms.</li>\n<li>Contact Form 7 forms.</li>\n<li>Mailchimp 4 WordPress forms.</li>\n<li>WPForms forms.</li>\n<li>WPForo new topic and reply forms.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>CAPTCHA can be individually enabled / disabled on each form.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A <strong>CAPTCHA</strong> test is designed to determine if an online user is really a human and not a bot. CAPTCHA is an acronym that stands for &#8220;Completely Automated Public Turing test to tell Computers and Humans Apart.&#8221;</p>\n</blockquote>\n",
        "installation": "<ul>\n<li>Go to your WordPress Dashboard.</li>\n<li>Click on Plugins -&gt; Add New</li>\n<li>Search form &#8220;<strong>Hizzle CAPTCHA</strong>&#8220;</li>\n<li>Find the plugin and click on the Install Now button</li>\n<li>After installation, click on Activate Plugin link to activate the plugin.</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"will%20this%20plugin%20work%20with%20version%203%20keys%3F\">\nWill this plugin work with version 3 keys?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>No. We only support version 2 keys for the time being.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"how%20can%20i%20get%20in%20touch%3F\">\nHow can I get in touch?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Use the <a href=\"https://support.noptin.com/help/1536964885\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">contact form on our website</a>.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"how%20can%20i%20contribute%20to%20hizzle%20captcha%3F\">\nHow can I contribute to Hizzle CAPTCHA?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>There are a lot of ways to contribute:-</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Suggest a feature via our <a href=\"https://support.noptin.com/help/1536964885\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">contact form</a>.</li>\n<li>Give us a <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/support/plugin/hizzle-recaptcha/reviews/?filter=5\" rel=\"ugc\">5* rating</a> on WordPress.</li>\n</ul>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"will%20this%20plugin%20work%20with%20my%20theme%3F\">\nWill this plugin work with my theme?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes, as long as your theme follows the WordPress theme development guidelines.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>2.0.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested on WordPress 6.9.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>2.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested on WordPress 6.7.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.1.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Test on WordPress 6.5.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.3</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Add ability to user alternative script source.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Compatibility with new Noptin forms editor.</li>\n<li>Bump tested WordPress version</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Get rid of spammers using this WordPress and WooCommerce CAPTCHA plugin for Google reCAPTCHA, Cloudflare Turnstile, and more.",
    "description": "<p><strong>This is a lightweight CAPTCHA plugin for WordPress and WooCommerce.</strong><br />\n★★★★★</p>\n<p>The free version supports the &#8220;I\\&#8217;m not a robot&#8221; Checkbox from Google reCAPTCHA.</p>\n<p>The premius version supports:-<br />\n&#8211; Invisible reCAPTCHA V2.<br />\n&#8211; Score based reCAPTCHA V3.<br />\n&#8211; Cloudflare Turnstile.</p>\n<p>Both versions allow you to protect your:-</p>\n<ul>\n<li>WordPress / WooCommerce login forms.</li>\n<li>WordPress / WooCommerce / BuddyPress registration forms.</li>\n<li>WordPress / WooCommerce lost password forms.</li>\n<li>WordPress / WooCommerce reset password forms.</li>\n<li>WordPress comment forms.</li>\n<li>WooCommerce checkout forms.</li>\n<li>Noptin newsletter subscription form.</li>\n<li>BBPress new topic and reply forms.</li>\n<li>BuddyPress new group forms.</li>\n<li>Contact Form 7 forms.</li>\n<li>Mailchimp 4 WordPress forms.</li>\n<li>WPForms forms.</li>\n<li>WPForo new topic and reply forms.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>CAPTCHA can be individually enabled / disabled on each form.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A <strong>CAPTCHA</strong> test is designed to determine if an online user is really a human and not a bot. CAPTCHA is an acronym that stands for &#8220;Completely Automated Public Turing test to tell Computers and Humans Apart.&#8221;</p>\n</blockquote>\n",
